                <pb facs="0896" n="760" sameAs="frus:frus1929v01/pg760"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">723.2515/3326: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Peru</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Moore</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Lima</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-04-09T15:00:00-05:00">April 9, 1929—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 7:10 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>62. Your 41, April 8, 2 p.m. President Leguia is at a loss to know how the
                    American engineers’ report could have been answered April <pb facs="0897"
                        n="761" xml:id="pg761"/> 4th by Chile when he did not deliver it to the
                    Chilean Ambassador here until April 6th.</p>
                <p>Engineer Seeley will today prepare an answer to the Chilean engineers’
                    statements.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Moore</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
